@startuml EagleViewArchitecture

title EagleView: AI-Powered Data Ingestion & Natural Language Analytics
caption Active FastAPI + Snowflake architecture | detailed request and response flow

skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing true
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam ParticipantPadding 18
skinparam BoxPadding 12
skinparam sequence {
  ArrowColor #2F80ED
  ActorBorderColor #5B9BD5
  ActorBackgroundColor #EAF3FF
  ParticipantBorderColor #8AA9C7
  ParticipantBackgroundColor #F5F9FE
  LifeLineBorderColor #B9D3EA
  LifeLineBackgroundColor #F9FCFF
  GroupBorderColor #6B6B6B
  GroupBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
  ReferenceBackgroundColor #FFF8DC
  ReferenceBorderColor #C8B458
  DividerBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
  DividerBorderColor #666666
}

actor "Business User" as user
participant "React Frontend\n(Vite / TypeScript)" as ui
participant "FastAPI Backend\n(Render)" as api
database "SQLite\nUser identities" as sqlite
database "Raw File Storage\nUploaded bytes" as files
participant "Snowpark Bridge\nShared session + user ctx" as bridge
database "Snowflake\nUser-scoped schemas" as sf
participant "Cortex\nStructured COMPLETE" as cortex
participant "Domain Cortex\nAgents" as agents
participant "SQL Validator\nRead-only firewall" as validator

== Data Onboarding & Ingestion Flow ==

user -> ui : Select CSV / Excel / JSON
ui -> api : POST /api/datasets/upload
api -> api : Verify Bearer JWT
api -> bridge : ready_context(user)
bridge -> sf : Create USER_<hash> schema
bridge -> sf : Ensure APP_* metadata tables
api -> api : Parse file into dataframe
api -> files : Save raw upload by dataset_id
api -> sf : Create APP_DATASETS row\nstatus = UPLOADED
sf --> api : dataset_id + row count
api --> ui : Upload accepted

ui -> api : POST /api/datasets/{id}/analyze
api -> files : Read saved raw upload
api -> sf : Mark dataset ANALYZING
api -> cortex : Orchestrator: split columns by domain
cortex --> api : Domain assignments

loop Each assigned domain slice
  api -> sf : Read existing target table columns
  api -> cortex : Classify slice + sample + live schema
  cortex --> api : Proposed mapping + confidence
  api -> sf : Save APP_DATASET_DOMAINS\nand APP_DATASET_COLUMNS
  api -> agents : Ask about ambiguous fields
  agents --> api : Optional agent note
end

api -> sf : Mark dataset SCHEMA_PROPOSED
api --> ui : Mappings + agent activity log
user -> ui : Review mappings and edit types
ui -> api : POST /api/datasets/{id}/confirm
api -> sf : Persist USER_MODIFIED mappings
api -> files : Read raw upload again
api -> sf : Mark dataset LOADING

loop Each confirmed domain
  api -> api : Select included columns\nand cast dataframe
  api -> agents : MergeDomainTable tool request
  agents -> sf : Create or extend persistent\ndomain table
  sf --> agents : Merge result
  api -> sf : write_pandas rows
  sf --> api : Loaded row count
  api -> sf : Mark domain READY
  api -> sf : Detect and save _ID relationships
end

api -> sf : Mark dataset READY
api --> ui : Loaded domains + row counts
ui --> user : Show ready data and dashboard entry

== Natural Language Analytics Flow ==

user -> ui : Ask a business question
ui -> api : POST /api/query\nquestion + optional session_id
api -> bridge : ready_context(user)
bridge -> sf : Load user-scoped metadata context
api -> sf : Save question in APP_CONVERSATIONS
api -> sf : List READY domains and table row counts

alt No READY domains
  sf --> api : No uploaded data
  api -> sf : Save no-data response
  api --> ui : Ask user to upload and confirm data
else Data is available
  api -> sf : Build catalog: tables, columns, relationships
  api -> sf : Load recent conversation history
  api -> cortex : Understand intent + entity + relevant tables
  cortex --> api : analytics / investigation / clarification

  alt Clarification required
    api -> sf : Save clarification response
    api --> ui : One short clarifying question
  else Analytics question
    api -> agents : Select primary relevant domain agent
    agents -> sf : RUN_SELECT_PROC\nGenerate and execute SELECT/WITH
    sf --> agents : Generated SQL + rows
    agents --> api : SQL + rows
  else Entity investigation
    par Relevant domains use independent Snowpark sessions
      api -> agents : Investigate order / customer / product
      agents -> sf : RUN_SELECT_PROC\nRead-only domain query
      sf --> agents : Domain SQL + rows
      agents --> api : Domain result
    end
  end

  api -> validator : Validate each returned SQL
  validator -> validator : One statement, SELECT/WITH only\nexact user schema + allowed tables

  alt Unsafe, unavailable, or no matching rows
    validator --> api : Reject or empty result
    api -> sf : Save unavailable / no-match response
    api --> ui : Standard empty-result response
  else Accepted rows
    validator --> api : Approved SQL + rows
    api -> cortex : Interpret rows + question + history
    cortex --> api : Answer + summary + timeline
    api -> sf : Save answer + generated SQL
    api --> ui : Answer, rows, SQL, timeline, agent log
    ui --> user : Render narrative and results
  end
end

== Authentication & Isolation Controls ==

user -> ui : Google sign-in or demo login
ui -> api : POST /api/auth/google or /demo
api -> sqlite : Lookup or create application user
api -> sqlite : Store user identity + schema name
api --> ui : Application JWT
ui -> api : Bearer JWT on every protected request
api -> bridge : Resolve authenticated user
bridge -> bridge : user_id -> USER_<sha256 hash>
bridge -> sf : Qualify every metadata and data query
validator -> sf : Enforce exact database/schema/table scope

note over sf
  Per-user Snowflake schema contains:
  APP_DATASETS, APP_DATASET_DOMAINS,
  APP_DATASET_COLUMNS, APP_RELATIONSHIPS,
  APP_CONVERSATIONS, and persistent domain tables.
end note

note over agents
  Active web path uses Snowflake Cortex Data Agents.
  backend/app/services Gemini modules remain a legacy /
  alternate path and are not imported by active routers.
end note

== Snowflake-Native Alternative ==

participant "Streamlit-in-Snowflake\nstreamlit_app.py" as streamlit
participant "Snowflake RBAC\nrbac.py / EXECUTE AS CALLER" as rbac

streamlit -> rbac : Resolve viewer context
rbac -> sf : Use same sf_lib pipeline\nwith caller-scoped access
streamlit -> sf : Upload, query, and render in Snowflake

legend right
  |= Visual convention |= Meaning |
  | Blue solid arrow | Request or command |
  | Dashed arrow | Response or returned data |
  | Yellow note | Important implementation boundary |
  | Group band | End-to-end user workflow |
endlegend
@enduml